course: dictionary
lesson: 1241
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning the writer means by reading the words around it, which is its context. «Bun» is one of these words: it can mean food or a hairstyle.
explain: Look at «hot cross bun», «burger bun» and «hair in a bun». The words next to bun are the clues. Hot cross and burger tell you it is food, a small round bread or a bread roll. Hair tells you it is a hairstyle, where long hair is twisted into a round knot.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense. If «Granny's pyRIzhky, little filled buns» is in the sentence, buns are food, so the meaning is bread.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Bun» means a small, round piece of bread, often sweet, as in «hot cross bun» or «cinnamon bun».
fact: «Bun» also means a bread roll used for a burger or hot dog, as in «burger bun».
fact: «Bun» can mean a hairstyle where long hair is twisted into a round knot, as in «hair in a bun».
fact: A word with more than one meaning can be understood by looking at the words around it.
exercise: «The bakery sold a warm cinnamon bun.» What is a bun here? | A bun for a burger | *A small, round sweet bread | A kind of bird | A knot of twisted hair
exercise: «She wore her hair in a bun for the dance.» What does bun mean here? | A bread roll | *A round knot of twisted hair | A small bread with raisins | A bun for a hot dog
exercise: «Tom put a sausage in his bun.» What is the clue that bun means food? | put | Tom | his | *sausage
exercise: «Granny baked little filled buns for the picnic.» What does bun mean? | *A little bread with a filling | A hairstyle | A small bird | A rope knot
exercise: «Mia pinned her long hair in a bun.» What does bun mean? | A bird's nest | A bread roll | A small sweet bread | *A round knot of twisted hair
test: «The burger bun was soft and warm.» What is a burger bun? | A small bird | *A bread roll for a burger | A round sweet bun with icing | A knot of hair
test: Which meaning of bun fits «hot cross bun» at Easter? | A bun for a hot dog | *A small, round, sweet bread | A hairstyle | A bird's nest
exam: «The bun was twisted at the back of her head.» Which meaning fits? | A bread roll for a burger | A small sweet bread | A kind of bird | *A hairstyle, a round knot of hair
